 ♪<i> On which we used to rely?</i> ♪

00:14.223 --> 00:17.850
 ♪<i> Lucky there's a family guy</i> ♪

00:18.001 --> 00:21.353
     ♪<i> Lucky there's a man</i>
    <i> who positively can do</i> ♪

00:21.505 --> 00:22.929
 ♪<i> All the things that make us</i> ♪

00:23.024 --> 00:24.581
       ♪<i> Laugh and cry</i> ♪

00:24.683 --> 00:30.154
        ♪<i> He's... a...</i>
     <i> Fam... ily... Guy!</i> ♪

00:35.986 --> 00:38.929
        (alarm beeping)

00:38.989 --> 00:40.330
          (alarm off)

00:41.917 --> 00:43.459
            (yawns)

00:46.330 --> 00:48.029
       (blows raspberry)

00:48.090 --> 00:50.215
   Alexa, what's in the news
         this morning?

00:50.367 --> 00:52.033
            <i> ALEXA:</i>
<i> Here is your morning briefing.</i>

00:52.053 --> 00:54.444
      <i> In Washington, D.C.,</i>
<i> Congress has passed a measure..</i>

00:54.463 --> 00:57.056
         Alexa, skip to
      celebrity birthdays.

00:57.224 --> 01:00.117
        <i> Mario Lopez is</i>
      <i> 47 years old today.</i>

01:00.177 --> 01:03.062
            No way!
 Someone should tell his face.

01:03.255 --> 01:04.788
        <i> I know, right?</i>

01:04.890 --> 01:06.456
          (chuckles):
          Seriously!

01:06.475 --> 01:08.901
  Okay, see you later, Alexa.

01:09.094 --> 01:11.144
     You're my best friend.

01:11.238 --> 01:13.980
         <i> And you're...</i>
     <i> you're awesome, Lois.</i>

01:14.133 --> 01:16.149
         Best friends.

01:16.243 --> 01:19.912
      MEG (calling out):
  Hey, Mom, my period started
         on the couch.

01:20.105 --> 01:21.154
      (takes deep breath)

01:22.416 --> 01:24.583
  You wanted to have a family,
     you wanted this life.

01:24.776 --> 01:27.068
   My shoes are on the roof.
           Get 'em.

01:27.088 --> 01:29.755
        (children's song
         playing on TV)

01:29.924 --> 01:32.240
  -♪<i> The driver on the bus peeks</i>
      <i> to check his phone</i> ♪
   -Come on, move your arm up.

01:32.259 --> 01:34.093
     -Up. Close your hand.
     -♪<i> Check his phone</i> ♪

01:34.286 --> 01:36.744
 -Okay, push it through. Good.
     -♪<i> Check his phone</i> ♪

01:36.764 --> 01:38.989
       -Just let me do it.
  -♪<i> The driver on the bus peeks</i>
      <i> to check his phone</i> ♪

01:39.007 --> 01:40.991
   -Other arm. Almost done.
   -♪<i> Whoops, he hit a dog</i> ♪

01:41.093 --> 01:43.936
        Move your thumb.
     Move your thumb. Push.

01:44.087 --> 01:45.604
         -There. Done.
   -♪<i> The driver on the bus</i> ♪

01:45.755 --> 01:47.589
   ♪<i> Says, "Shut up, shut up,</i>
           <i> shut up</i> ♪

01:47.608 --> 01:51.001
 ♪<i> Let me think for a second."</i> ♪

01:51.019 --> 01:52.519
        (Lois straining)

01:52.655 --> 01:54.113
      Why did you do this?

01:54.306 --> 01:56.189
    If they didn't want us
  to put our foot down there,

01:56.325 --> 01:59.343
     they shouldn't make it
a perfect fit for a toilet shoe.

01:59.361 --> 02:01.528
         -Who's "they"?
        -Uh, Big Toilet?

02:01.622 --> 02:03.622
         "Big Toilet"?
        Is that a thing?

02:03.773 --> 02:05.457
              Shh!

02:05.650 --> 02:07.126
     <i> MAN: Welcome back to</i>
<i> the</i> Stuff You Should Just Spend

02:07.277 --> 02:08.961
     the Money On<i> podcast.</i>

02:09.112 --> 02:11.797
   <i> Today's episode: "Expressing</i>
     <i> Your Dog's Anal Glands."</i>

02:11.948 --> 02:14.691
<i>MAN 2: Yeah, you really don't</i>
<i>want to DIY on the anal glands.</i>

02:14.751 --> 02:16.618
    <i> Just spend the money.</i>
   <i> It can't cost more than,</i>

02:16.720 --> 02:18.620
   <i> -I don't know, 30 bucks.</i>
        -(Brian grunts)

02:18.722 --> 02:20.864
   <i> -MAN: $30 is three months</i>
          <i> of Netflix.</i>
           -(grunts)

02:20.883 --> 02:22.624
    <i> MAN 2: So don't watch</i>
  The Crown<i> for three months.</i>

02:22.726 --> 02:25.051
       -I like<i> The Crown.</i>
<i> -MAN: What if I like</i> The Crown?

02:25.204 --> 02:26.887
     <i> -MAN 2: Watch it all</i>
       <i> in one weekend.</i>
       -(both grunting)

02:26.981 --> 02:29.055
     <i> If you don't finish</i>
<i> a Netflix series in a weekend,</i>

02:29.191 --> 02:31.057
       <i> -that's on you.</i>
     -Lois, can we just...

02:31.193 --> 02:32.893
can we just kiss a little first?

02:33.045 --> 02:34.636
          You know what?
  I think it's actually starting

02:34.655 --> 02:36.804
    to clear up on its own.
     ♪<i> Whoa, Black Betty</i> ♪

02:36.824 --> 02:38.157
 ♪<i> Bam-a-lam, hey, Black Betty</i> ♪

02:38.325 --> 02:39.491
         ♪<i> Bam-a-lam!</i> ♪

02:39.684 --> 02:41.952
               ♪

02:45.449 --> 02:47.724
         -(horn honks)
       -(Lois honks back)

02:47.826 --> 02:51.253
   Take a bite out of my ass,
       you sack of dirt!

02:54.032 --> 02:55.990
     (mellow music playing)

02:56.010 --> 02:57.176
        (inhales deeply)

02:57.369 --> 03:00.262
       Ah... you made it.

03:01.390 --> 03:04.090
  Morning, Kyle, Lisa, Kyle H.

03:04.185 --> 03:05.517
         Morning, Lois.

03:05.669 --> 03:07.186
  What'll it be this morning?
          The usual?

03:07.354 --> 03:09.337
       Ah, you know it.
  And with the morning I had,

03:09.398 --> 03:10.931
    better make it a large.

03:11.025 --> 03:13.508
         So the usual.

03:13.527 --> 03:15.677
      How are the muffins
      this morning, Lisa?

03:15.738 --> 03:18.422
 Oh, not the banana nut, 'cause
 I know you're allergic to nuts.

03:18.482 --> 03:20.424
(chuckles): That's right, I am.
         Good memory.

03:20.484 --> 03:22.183
   Well, it's what makes you
          so unique.

03:22.203 --> 03:23.702
             MAN:
           Hurry up!

03:23.895 --> 03:25.853
   You know, I always thought
     that peanut allergies

03:25.873 --> 03:27.855
        just went away
   when you became an adult.

03:27.917 --> 03:29.115
    You know, like tonsils.

03:29.268 --> 03:30.358
    Tonsils go away, right?

03:30.461 --> 03:31.952
     I thought I read that.

03:32.046 --> 03:33.045
       What are tonsils?

03:33.238 --> 03:35.105
 Anyway, let me put in my card.

03:35.165 --> 03:36.790
  I got one with a chip on it.

03:36.884 --> 03:39.459
     It's like we're living
       in the<i> Star Wars.</i>

03:39.553 --> 03:40.961
           Okay, tip.

03:41.055 --> 03:42.221
         I'll do cash.

03:42.389 --> 03:43.780
      Good, you heard me.

03:43.840 --> 03:46.116
   "Would you like to donate
        a cup of coffee

03:46.176 --> 03:47.784
    to a soldier overseas?"

03:47.844 --> 03:50.787
     Yeah, that seems like
         a good cause.

03:50.847 --> 03:52.956
     MAN: Hey. Here's your
      free cup of coffee

03:53.058 --> 03:55.317
 -from a lady in Rhode Island.
            -What?

04:01.450 --> 04:02.574
               ♪

04:21.453 --> 04:24.078
   Excuse me. Are you in line
       for the bathroom?

04:24.139 --> 04:25.822
              -No.
              -Oh.

04:25.924 --> 04:27.432
           Then move!

04:27.584 --> 04:30.352
      -(rattles doorknob)
       -Give me the key!

04:33.190 --> 04:35.774
  So, how was everybody's day?

04:35.967 --> 04:38.259
  -I made the football team...
       -Congratulations.

04:38.320 --> 04:41.171
   ...throw up because I put
   cleaner in the Gatorade.

04:41.231 --> 04:42.447
       Still pretty good.

04:43.842 --> 04:45.933
  You know, the funniest thing
     happened to me today.

04:45.995 --> 04:48.011
    I go to this coffee shop
         every morning,

04:48.030 --> 04:49.937
   and they do this fun thing
        where every week

04:49.999 --> 04:51.939
          they choose
    a Customer of the Week.

04:51.959 --> 04:54.184
   It's just a silly thing,
   which is why it's so fun.

04:54.286 --> 04:56.202
 Anyway, I've never been picked.

04:56.297 --> 04:58.188
         Which is fine.

04:58.248 --> 04:59.856
        The thing is...

04:59.958 --> 05:00.948
            Oh, boy.

05:00.968 --> 05:02.634
 ...I'm friendly, I always tip,

05:02.827 --> 05:06.046
  I almost never say anything
when foreigners loudly FaceTime,

05:06.140 --> 05:09.032
        and in general,
   I'm a pretty good person.

05:09.051 --> 05:10.291
             Right?

05:10.352 --> 05:12.460
         Yeah. I mean,
    you show little patience

05:12.479 --> 05:15.147
 for the handicapped at times,
         but... yeah.

05:15.340 --> 05:16.890
         Yeah, it just,
       it just feels like

05:17.026 --> 05:18.633
 it should probably be my time.

05:18.694 --> 05:20.152
     Well, maybe this'll be
           your week.

05:20.345 --> 05:21.486
       Oh, you think so?

05:21.679 --> 05:22.988
         I don't know.
      That-that felt like

05:23.181 --> 05:24.381
    the right thing to say,
         so I said it.

05:24.399 --> 05:25.973
     I do impulsive things.

05:25.993 --> 05:28.735
 That's how I ended up getting
      Rod Stewart's hair.

05:28.887 --> 05:30.220
         Morning, luv.

05:30.322 --> 05:32.831
     Mind if I sing a tune
       into your vagina?

05:33.024 --> 05:35.876
               ♪

05:37.254 --> 05:39.896
           Everybody,
if we could have your attention,

05:40.007 --> 05:43.175
   we'd like to announce this
  week's Customer of the Week.

05:43.368 --> 05:45.344
    Ah. I've never seen them
     do it live. (chuckles)

05:45.495 --> 05:48.263
This must be what it feels like
         to see Bruce.

05:49.683 --> 05:53.410
          This week's
   Customer of the Week is...

05:53.470 --> 05:55.062
            Lester!

05:56.523 --> 05:58.523
               ♪

06:06.558 --> 06:09.034
           (sobbing)

06:11.288 --> 06:13.372
        (sobbing loudly)

06:19.046 --> 06:21.271
           Hey, Bon,
    Wednesday Wisdom's live!

06:21.289 --> 06:23.030
          -Is it good?
              -No.

06:23.092 --> 06:24.508
          It's great!

06:30.799 --> 06:32.724
     You know what I think
    the problem is, Stewie?

06:32.876 --> 06:34.226
      I need to show them

06:34.335 --> 06:36.210
     that I deserve to be
     Customer of the Week.

06:36.230 --> 06:38.212
          -You don't.
    -Well, they probably see
   a woman like me and think,

06:38.315 --> 06:40.140
      -"She's got it all."
          -They don't.

06:40.234 --> 06:42.142
          I know it's
     a silly little award,

06:42.236 --> 06:44.069
   -but I don't ask for much.
            -You do.

06:44.220 --> 06:45.553
   And this is the one place,

06:45.656 --> 06:47.830
         the one place
   that makes me feel happy.

06:47.832 --> 06:49.966
         -You aren't.
      -I don't understand
     what I'm doing wrong.

06:50.026 --> 06:52.318
  I-I feel like I really vibe
     with everyone there.

06:52.454 --> 06:54.320
          -You don't.
            -I'm one
    of their best customers.

06:54.456 --> 06:56.156
           You know,
    if I stopped showing up,

06:56.250 --> 06:57.582
     they'd probably wonder
         where I went.

06:57.775 --> 06:59.751
        -They wouldn't.
  -Because I'm a nice person.

06:59.920 --> 07:01.235
         -You're not.
        -I tip in cash.

07:01.296 --> 07:03.088
              -So?
-And I can't think of one reason

07:03.281 --> 07:04.998
  -why they wouldn't pick me.
            -I can.

07:05.092 --> 07:06.166
   Oh, thanks for listening,
            Stewie.

07:07.410 --> 07:08.652
        -I had no choice.
  -You know, I'm gonna show them

07:08.670 --> 07:10.244
     that I deserve to win
          this award.

07:10.305 --> 07:12.246
         I need this--
       just like I needed

07:12.307 --> 07:15.082
         my own Gregor
    "The Mountain" Clegane.

07:15.185 --> 07:16.751
            -Next.
           -Hi, Gil.

07:16.854 --> 07:17.510
        Uh, can I get...

07:18.439 --> 07:19.679
      Pound of honey ham.
         Cut it thin.

07:19.831 --> 07:21.255
        Oh, excuse me,
     I believe I was next.

07:21.358 --> 07:23.442
       Step aside, lady.

07:28.023 --> 07:29.355
         Yeah, hi, Gil.

07:29.508 --> 07:31.933
       Can I try a piece
     of the pepper turkey?

07:31.952 --> 07:34.119
               ♪

07:37.073 --> 07:38.623
          Here you go.
      Anything else today?

07:38.816 --> 07:40.775
       Yeah, the coffee,
       and you know what?

07:40.794 --> 07:43.203
I'll take that piece of artwork
     for sale on the wall.

07:43.297 --> 07:45.205
  Really? That's my painting.

07:45.299 --> 07:47.023
         Wha...? Is it?

07:47.083 --> 07:48.967
     You are very talented.

07:49.160 --> 07:51.211
  Well, how much do I owe you?

07:51.305 --> 07:54.806
            -$600.
        -(chokes) $600?

07:54.999 --> 07:55.974
     Do you still want it?

07:56.143 --> 07:56.975
           Of course.

07:57.126 --> 07:58.384
         (quiet grunt)

07:58.520 --> 08:00.127
   It's important to support
         local artists

08:00.230 --> 08:02.129
          by spending
   a year's worth of co-pays

08:02.191 --> 08:04.057
     on a painting of a...
       (chokes, belches)

08:04.193 --> 08:05.391
       (pounding counter)

08:05.486 --> 08:06.376
           ...bridge.

08:06.436 --> 08:08.153
     A ladder and an apple.

08:08.322 --> 08:11.064
     A ladder and an apple!
         What a theme!

08:11.158 --> 08:13.049
       Can you split it
      on two debit cards?

08:13.068 --> 08:15.977
        -I have a limit.
   -I can't really ring it up
        on the register.

08:16.038 --> 08:18.205
      -It has to be cash.
           -(chokes)

08:19.374 --> 08:20.890
            Perfect!

08:20.951 --> 08:23.084
               ♪

08:26.698 --> 08:28.507
    -By the way, I told you.
         -Told me what?

08:28.700 --> 08:30.509
       I told you nobody
   could tell I was drinking.

08:30.702 --> 08:33.253
        -No one cares.
        -I care.<i> I</i>  do.

08:34.723 --> 08:37.832
Here, take this. Start recording
 right before they say my name.

08:37.851 --> 08:39.759
     And hold it landscape,
         not portrait.

08:39.853 --> 08:42.262
 This is an important moment,
 not a fast-food worker fight.

08:42.414 --> 08:44.523
          (quietly):
         I wish it was
   a fast-food worker fight.

08:44.691 --> 08:48.101
            -What?
   -(loudly): I wish it<i> was</i>
   a fast-food worker fight.

08:48.195 --> 08:49.528
      Welcome, everybody.

08:49.721 --> 08:52.531
          This week's
   Customer of the Week is...

08:53.525 --> 08:55.951
     ...Terry Newcustomer.

08:57.746 --> 09:02.098
  Wow, this is so unexpected,
because I'm such a new customer.

09:02.117 --> 09:03.283
 Lois, should I stop recording?

09:03.377 --> 09:04.784
      Oh, you got a text.

09:04.878 --> 09:06.027
       Oh, I clicked it.

09:06.046 --> 09:06.878
        Oh, it's Bonnie.

09:07.030 --> 09:08.380
    She's responding to you.

09:08.573 --> 09:10.790
          Oh, about me.
  Oh, I'm reading the old texts.

09:10.884 --> 09:11.916
       Oh, I should stop.

09:12.052 --> 09:12.884
        Oh, but I can't.

09:13.053 --> 09:14.052
      Oh, you're unhappy.

09:14.245 --> 09:15.220
        Oh, who's Greg?

09:15.389 --> 09:17.113
       Oh, there's Greg.

09:17.173 --> 09:19.040
               ♪

09:19.935 --> 09:22.969
  All right, on three, everyone
  say their favorite Spider-Man.

09:23.121 --> 09:25.230
  All right? One, two, three.

09:25.423 --> 09:27.048
  (saying different Spider-Man
     characters and actors)

09:27.067 --> 09:28.049
         ALL BUT LOIS:
            What?!

09:29.260 --> 09:31.111
      (Meg, Chris, Peter,
   Brian and Stewie arguing)

09:32.990 --> 09:35.907
In fact, there'd be no superhero
 movies without Tobey Maguire.

09:36.100 --> 09:38.743
            No way!
  Garfield never got a chance.

09:38.895 --> 09:40.061
  Is Affleck the best Batman?

09:40.080 --> 09:41.413
        No. But he had
     the best Batman body.

09:41.564 --> 09:44.082
He'll be the first ex-Spider-Man
        to win an Oscar.

09:44.233 --> 09:46.859
  Just 'cause it's in animation,
   people think it's not legit.

09:46.920 --> 09:49.588
      (indistinct arguing)

09:50.632 --> 09:52.332
               ♪

09:52.426 --> 09:55.010
   (others continue arguing)

10:00.124 --> 10:01.766
        I don't get it!

10:01.959 --> 10:02.992
       Wait, Spider-Man?

10:03.053 --> 10:04.344
 He's a guy with spider powers.

10:04.438 --> 10:06.087
     Can't I have one thing
          in my life?

10:06.148 --> 10:07.180
    Is that too much to ask?

10:07.274 --> 10:08.756
  What is it, do they hate me?

10:08.817 --> 10:11.017
     Because astrologically
      I'm very compatible

10:11.153 --> 10:13.019
     with Kyle H. and Lisa.

10:13.155 --> 10:15.021
          I'm a Gemini
   and they're both Aquarius,

10:15.157 --> 10:16.764
   so we're natural matches!

10:16.825 --> 10:18.766
        Kyle is a Virgo,
which doesn't match with Gemini,

10:18.827 --> 10:21.194
       but they're supposed
  to at least care about people!

10:21.346 --> 10:22.787
       What am I missing?

10:22.980 --> 10:24.956
     You know, Mom, if you
  really want to get noticed,

10:25.125 --> 10:26.941
        you should save
      one of their lives.

10:27.002 --> 10:28.793
             -What?
   -There was a kid at school

10:28.945 --> 10:31.187
      who got a whole page
in the yearbook dedicated to him

10:31.289 --> 10:34.190
    because he saved a kid
   who had a peanut allergy.

10:34.292 --> 10:36.359
        Peanut allergy?

10:36.378 --> 10:38.044
    I have a peanut allergy.

10:38.196 --> 10:41.865
Yeah. This kid accidentally ate
 something with peanuts in it

10:41.925 --> 10:43.549
  and the other kid came over

10:43.644 --> 10:45.718
     and<i> Pulp Fictioned</i> him
        with an EpiPen.

10:45.854 --> 10:46.811
             Huh...

10:47.004 --> 10:48.705
  I can't even touch peanuts.

10:48.723 --> 10:51.040
      That kid was a hero.

10:51.101 --> 10:52.558
            Hero...

10:52.711 --> 10:53.801
         You flush it!

10:53.862 --> 10:55.528
 It scares me when it goes away.

10:57.107 --> 10:58.398
          Yes... hero.

10:58.492 --> 10:59.382
        I'll be a hero,

11:00.702 --> 11:02.218
     and then they'll have
to make me Customer of the Week.

11:02.320 --> 11:03.736
       Why is this story
    all about Mom this week?

11:03.830 --> 11:06.956
      What, are we giving
      Seth's voice a rest?

11:12.288 --> 11:15.256
  (electric guitar riff plays)

11:20.872 --> 11:24.165
       Okay, I'll just pour
  some of these Planters peanuts

11:24.226 --> 11:25.833
        into Lisa's car.

11:25.852 --> 11:27.093
      The official peanut

11:27.187 --> 11:28.761
          of poisoning
     people with allergies.

11:28.855 --> 11:30.855
    What? No, she's kidding!

11:31.007 --> 11:32.265
      Come on, look at me:

11:32.359 --> 11:34.767
    top hat, gloves, shoes,
       no other clothes.

11:34.920 --> 11:36.194
        I'm a good guy!

11:36.387 --> 11:39.346
       Okay, now I wait
   for her to get in her car

11:39.408 --> 11:41.274
 and start to have a reaction.

11:41.426 --> 11:44.185
        Then I'll swoop in
  and save her with this EpiPen.

11:44.246 --> 11:46.871
      Then I'll be a lock
  to be Customer of the Week.

11:47.064 --> 11:49.023
  Stewie, you okay back there?

11:49.084 --> 11:51.192
      Having fun playing
      with Mommy's phone?

11:51.253 --> 11:53.269
           Yup. I put
   the headphones up my nose,

11:53.329 --> 11:55.004
      but I made it work.

11:56.883 --> 11:58.274
      Okay, there she is.

11:58.293 --> 12:00.051
  She's walking to her car...

12:00.244 --> 12:01.794
 she's getting out her keys...

12:01.930 --> 12:03.537
   she's starting her car...

12:03.598 --> 12:05.140
         driving away?

12:08.887 --> 12:12.230
     Damn it, I didn't put
    enough peanuts in there.

12:13.900 --> 12:15.233
       Oh, shaving cream!

12:16.653 --> 12:19.279
      Ooh, shaving cream.

12:22.025 --> 12:23.908
             Oh...

12:24.101 --> 12:26.202
         shaving cream.

12:30.533 --> 12:31.458
           Oh, good.

12:32.294 --> 12:34.085
       Oh, shaving cream.

12:40.761 --> 12:44.153
Mom, why are we at the hospital
    to visit your barista?

12:44.255 --> 12:46.656
        Chris, I promise
  that if one of your baristas

12:46.758 --> 12:49.492
  ever gets into an accident,
 I'll go to the hospital, too.

12:49.511 --> 12:51.160
             Okay.
  That's all I wanted to hear.

12:51.179 --> 12:54.347
    I've got a lot of baristas
  who make questionable choices.

12:54.441 --> 12:57.424
 Hi, you must be Lisa's mother.

12:57.444 --> 12:58.351
        How's she doing?

12:58.445 --> 13:00.186
   Did she say what happened?

13:00.322 --> 13:02.763
 No, she's mostly just said...

13:02.824 --> 13:04.357
       (ghastly moaning)

13:04.451 --> 13:06.284
  Oh, that's not a good moan.

13:06.477 --> 13:09.103
        Well, apparently,
  someone put peanuts in her car

13:09.122 --> 13:10.847
  and she's deathly allergic.

13:10.907 --> 13:12.015
            Oh, no.

13:12.075 --> 13:13.625
       Here are flowers.

13:13.776 --> 13:15.776
            STEWIE:
         She took those
   from a guardrail memorial.

13:15.837 --> 13:18.021
  D-Do they have any leads on
    who could have done it?

13:18.081 --> 13:18.871
              No.

13:19.024 --> 13:20.540
          Good. Grief!

13:20.634 --> 13:22.801
     "Good grief," is what
 Charlie Brown would say here.

13:22.994 --> 13:24.952
      <i> Peanuts.</i> Probably
  a poor choice of reference.

13:25.013 --> 13:27.363
  But they're going to check the
  parking lot surveillance tape

13:27.382 --> 13:28.306
        to see who did.

13:28.499 --> 13:30.883
 Surveillance tape? Good grief!

13:31.019 --> 13:32.293
     Uh, who are you again?

13:32.354 --> 13:34.887
 I'm a... a very good customer.

13:35.023 --> 13:36.463
  Oh, my God, I've got to go.

13:36.525 --> 13:38.525
        Exit stage left!

13:40.695 --> 13:44.405
    That was a very sad door
         to run in to.

13:55.168 --> 13:57.418
      What the hell? Lois?

14:00.048 --> 14:02.131
             LOIS:
  Put the phone down, Kyle H.

14:04.052 --> 14:05.251
           ...so then
   I start hearing people say

14:05.387 --> 14:06.919
   there are different levels

14:07.072 --> 14:08.588
      of peanut allergies
   and I was like, "Levels?"

14:08.682 --> 14:11.182
  I mean, when I hear allergy,
         I think rash,

14:11.375 --> 14:13.334
  not throat-close-car-crash.

14:13.395 --> 14:16.412
   Okay, well, I-I'm so glad
 that we could talk about this

14:16.472 --> 14:19.190
    and that you understand
  how we got to where we are.

14:19.342 --> 14:20.766
  So, are you gonna let me go?

14:20.861 --> 14:21.767
              Yes.

14:23.012 --> 14:23.936
   I mean, once I figure out
     this whole kerfuffle.

14:24.030 --> 14:25.088
              Oh.

14:25.189 --> 14:27.198
 Why, are you scared, Kyle H.?

14:27.391 --> 14:30.017
       This isn't scary.

14:30.078 --> 14:31.703
       I'm a good person.

14:31.854 --> 14:34.038
    Now, there are two ways
     we can go from here:

14:34.231 --> 14:36.099
        you can give me
      your absolute trust,

14:36.159 --> 14:38.918
    or I can get you hooked
          on heroin.

14:39.070 --> 14:40.286
       Heroin's not bad.

14:40.380 --> 14:43.289
       Not having heroin,
       that's what's bad.

14:43.441 --> 14:45.884
Y-You can trust me. It's just...

14:46.052 --> 14:47.034
           Just what?

14:47.095 --> 14:48.277
         I have a cat.

14:48.338 --> 14:49.888
   Someone needs to feed him.

14:50.056 --> 14:52.557
         (long inhale)

14:52.726 --> 14:56.135
       Now, a bad person
  would say "who cares" here.

14:56.287 --> 14:58.804
 But since I am a good person,

14:58.899 --> 15:00.714
 I will take care of your cat.

15:00.775 --> 15:02.383
     Now, open your mouth,
        I'm gonna stuff

15:02.444 --> 15:04.277
 my son's baseball sock in it.

15:15.081 --> 15:17.081
  What the hell? Who are you?

15:17.233 --> 15:18.324
           Oh, hello.

15:18.460 --> 15:22.086
            Um, hi,
   I'm Kyle H.'s cat-sitter.

15:22.255 --> 15:24.480
       He didn't tell me
       he had roommates

15:24.499 --> 15:26.573
 who could feed his cat for him.

15:26.635 --> 15:29.168
     Wait, why do you have
       his laser pointer

15:29.320 --> 15:30.987
    and Heisenberg keychain?

15:31.089 --> 15:33.839
Yeah, his keychain flair is how
 he expresses his quirkiness.

15:33.934 --> 15:35.391
     He must be in danger!

15:40.357 --> 15:42.256
       You can't leave us
        like this, lady.

15:42.359 --> 15:43.274
       Don't say "lady."

15:43.467 --> 15:45.001
     It makes me feel old.

15:45.019 --> 15:47.019
   And why is everyone acting
     like this is my fault?

15:47.113 --> 15:49.338
         If anything,
     it's Kyle H.'s fault.

15:49.399 --> 15:51.174
       I'm a good person.

15:51.234 --> 15:52.617
     People are gonna know
          we're gone.

15:52.810 --> 15:54.101
    I promised my boyfriend
          that I'd...

15:54.162 --> 15:55.528
       -Wait, you're gay?
             -Yeah.

15:55.622 --> 15:56.679
      You sound surprised.

15:57.849 --> 15:58.623
          I don't know,
  you just don't present as gay.

15:58.792 --> 16:00.016
     Oh, so gays "present"?

16:00.076 --> 16:01.367
    No, no, no, that's not--

16:01.519 --> 16:03.294
     What? I'm woke, okay?

16:03.487 --> 16:04.537
     Is he your boyfriend?

16:04.631 --> 16:05.855
        No, I'm not gay.

16:05.915 --> 16:07.540
  What? But you're roommates.

16:07.634 --> 16:09.283
             -So?
             -So?!

16:09.302 --> 16:10.284
     And that's not weird?

16:11.346 --> 16:12.619
      I mean, do you have
      your own bathrooms?

16:12.681 --> 16:14.621
               -No.
  -What, so you just walk around

16:14.641 --> 16:16.215
     -like there's nothing
      potentially sexual?
            -Yeah.

16:16.309 --> 16:18.309
         Yeah. I mean,
 ever since he joined the gym,

16:18.502 --> 16:19.978
       he's really turned
        his body around.

16:20.129 --> 16:21.646
      But that's not what
      I'd be attracted to.

16:21.797 --> 16:24.056
      It's more sticking to
  his commitment to get healthy.

16:24.150 --> 16:26.150
      -That's attractive.
      -Aw, thank you, bro.

16:26.319 --> 16:27.226
    Mm, you're welcome, bro.

16:27.378 --> 16:28.728
           See, this!

16:28.822 --> 16:31.138
         I don't know.
 I-I guess I'm not woke, okay?

16:31.199 --> 16:33.216
         Fine, you win
      with your gay stuff.

16:33.276 --> 16:35.051
     That's what you want,
        right? To win?

16:35.069 --> 16:38.404
    Here, drink whatever you
think a day's worth of water is.

16:38.556 --> 16:40.223
    Look, what I was trying
        to say is that

16:40.241 --> 16:42.892
 you can't leave us like this
because I promised my boyfriend

16:42.910 --> 16:44.818
   that I'd make a meal for
 his grandmother's meal train.

16:44.879 --> 16:47.821
If I don't drop it off, they're
 gonna know something's wrong.

16:47.882 --> 16:50.750
         (long inhale)

16:50.885 --> 16:52.084
           (exhales)

16:52.178 --> 16:53.660
 What are you supposed to make?

16:53.722 --> 16:56.180
       -Beef Wellington.
   -What-- Beef Wellington?!

16:56.373 --> 16:57.831
         -For tonight?
          -Yeah, why?

16:57.892 --> 16:59.350
         -Is that hard?
             -Yes!

16:59.502 --> 17:03.021
       If you're starting
    at 2:00 p.m., very! Yes!

17:08.186 --> 17:09.919
      Lois, have you seen
       the pooping iPad?

17:09.979 --> 17:12.104
         I can only go
  while watching<i> Tiger King</i> .

17:12.257 --> 17:13.773
             -Huh?
     -The iPad we use only

17:13.867 --> 17:16.592
  while pooping and occasionally
      on flights for Stewie.

17:16.652 --> 17:19.595
 Ew, I play<i> Elmo's ABCs</i> on that.

17:19.614 --> 17:21.873
          Is that why
    I keep getting pink eye?

17:22.934 --> 17:24.100
   I don't know where it is.

17:24.118 --> 17:25.376
    But it's definitely not
         in the shed.

17:25.569 --> 17:27.027
      So don't even look
    back there in the shed.

17:27.088 --> 17:29.029
        What, you mean
the earwig fortress? No thanks.

17:29.049 --> 17:30.456
    I haven't been in there

17:30.550 --> 17:31.865
     since I won the Battle
      of the Wheelbarrow.

17:31.885 --> 17:33.217
            Nyah-ha!

17:33.410 --> 17:36.220
     Too fast and too smart
       for you, earwigs.

17:37.673 --> 17:40.449
        Now, to continue
      clearing the yard...

17:40.468 --> 17:44.303
          (monotone):
     ...collecting moisture
     and sleeping in wood.

17:44.455 --> 17:46.046
          Hey, Lois,
     what ever happened to

17:46.066 --> 17:47.714
   -that Customer of the Week
             thing?
         -Th-the what?

17:47.734 --> 17:49.292
    The Customer of the Week
      at the coffee shop.

17:49.352 --> 17:50.551
       Did you ever win?

17:50.612 --> 17:52.070
       Why? Why would you
         bring that up?

17:52.221 --> 17:53.479
         What are you,
       obsessed with it?

17:53.631 --> 17:55.147
           Uh, you--
you had been talking about it...

17:55.241 --> 17:56.966
     Oh, so you can hear me
        when I say that,

17:56.984 --> 17:58.818
       but can't hear me
when I say "get off the couch."

17:58.953 --> 18:00.319
   I like to be up by people.

18:00.455 --> 18:02.580
     May I be excused to...

18:02.773 --> 18:06.375
          (monotone):
  bring this plate of moisture
      to the crawl space?

18:08.329 --> 18:09.979
     Yeah, for the record,

18:10.039 --> 18:11.147
        I would rather
    drink a sinus infection

18:11.207 --> 18:12.256
  than win that stupid award.

18:12.408 --> 18:13.499
    It's all rigged anyway.

18:15.044 --> 18:16.743
  Did you know that Lester lived
  in the same building as Lisa?

18:16.763 --> 18:18.487
     How is that fair, huh?

18:18.506 --> 18:21.006
   God, what a boring thing
 to bring up at dinner, Brian.

18:21.159 --> 18:22.842
   I'm going to the sunroom,

18:22.936 --> 18:25.828
 and that's where I'll be from
 9:00 to 11:00 if anyone asks.

18:25.888 --> 18:27.421
    No one come check on me.

18:28.833 --> 18:31.216
   You guys want to play spin
  the bottle for finger stuff?

18:31.319 --> 18:33.018
  Crank this night up a notch?

18:33.113 --> 18:35.113
            I'm in.

18:37.358 --> 18:38.765
         <i> Good evening.</i>
        <i> I'm Tom Tucker.</i>

18:38.785 --> 18:40.767
        <i> In local news,</i>
   <i> two roommates were found</i>

18:40.787 --> 18:42.678
       <i> bound and gagged in</i>
   <i> their apartment this morning</i>

18:42.738 --> 18:45.790
   <i> in what they're calling,</i>
<i> "The Cat-Sitter Tie-er Upper."</i>

18:45.941 --> 18:48.367
  <i> Guys, we need to get better</i>
   <i> name-comer-upper-withers.</i>

18:48.461 --> 18:51.087
               ♪

18:52.957 --> 18:55.374
     (sirens wail faintly)

18:55.468 --> 18:57.552
               ♪

19:12.527 --> 19:14.110
             Okay.

19:17.991 --> 19:19.323
   (indistinct radio chatter)

19:19.475 --> 19:20.566
             Lois?

19:20.660 --> 19:23.068
       I'm just finishing
          the dishes.

19:23.163 --> 19:25.221
    I'm a good person, Joe.

19:25.323 --> 19:27.890
     Sometimes good people
     do bad things, Lois.

19:27.992 --> 19:29.392
   You can finish the dishes.

19:29.493 --> 19:31.151
   Then I gotta take you in.

19:31.212 --> 19:33.078
 You can't take her away, Joe!

19:33.173 --> 19:34.747
          (whispering)

19:34.899 --> 19:36.323
       And you can put in
      one load of laundry.

19:36.426 --> 19:38.009
   Then I gotta take you in.

19:38.160 --> 19:39.510
          (whispering)

19:39.703 --> 19:41.904
   After that, you can write
    down the Wi-Fi log-in.

19:41.964 --> 19:43.848
   Then I gotta take you in.

19:44.041 --> 19:45.090
          (whispering)

19:45.226 --> 19:46.833
   Where's the peanut butter?

19:46.853 --> 19:48.260
          (whispering)

19:48.354 --> 19:49.912
      Well, Peter, I think
     the main difference is

19:49.972 --> 19:51.414
 Chinese people are from China

19:51.474 --> 19:53.582
      and Japanese people
        are from Japan.

19:53.684 --> 19:54.508
          (whispering)

19:56.053 --> 19:57.987
  Yes, that's probably why you
were banned from the restaurant.

20:04.195 --> 20:07.096
               ♪

20:07.156 --> 20:09.332
               ♪

20:27.343 --> 20:29.301
         Good morning.

20:29.454 --> 20:31.620
   Ah, what a charming place
           this is.

20:31.681 --> 20:34.123
       Oh, look, you do
    a Customer of the Week.

20:34.183 --> 20:35.382
           How cute.

20:35.443 --> 20:38.885
         Now, I'll take
       a Nitro Cold Brew.

20:38.947 --> 20:41.797
  And with the morning I've had,
     better make it a large.

20:41.857 --> 20:43.223
       Hey, that's funny.

20:43.284 --> 20:45.076
         Yeah, I know.

20:45.227 --> 20:47.119
         There you go.

20:48.030 --> 20:50.639
       And there you go.

20:50.700 --> 20:53.233
   Well, you could have said
          thank you.

20:53.294 --> 20:55.902
      Don't see a lot of
  five dollar bills in there.

20:55.964 --> 20:59.507
  I must be a pretty good person
         to give a five.